# Runtime dependency inputs for the v100-qwen-image GPU stack (task M0.1).
#
# Target: Linux x86_64, CPython 3.11 and 3.13. The *lockfile* (requirements.lock)
# carries the fully resolved transitive pins; this file carries only direct
# requirements and the index assumptions.
#
# Index assumptions:
#   * torch MUST come from the official cu126 wheel index. PyPI's plain
#     `torch` and any cu13x build are wrong for this build: the cu126 series
#     (<= 2.14) is the last publishing cu126 and the last to ship sm_70
#     (Volta) kernels. The +cu126 local version label only exists on
#     download.pytorch.org, so the exact pin below cannot silently fall back
#     to a plain-PyPI or cu13 wheel.
#   * Everything else resolves from PyPI. IMPORTANT: uv must be run with
#     `--index-strategy unsafe-best-match` (a CLI-only flag; uv 0.12.1 does
#     not accept it inside a requirements file). With uv's default
#     first-index strategy the torch extra index takes precedence over PyPI
#     and drags in the stale mirrors it hosts (certifi 2022.12.7,
#     requests 2.28.1, urllib3 1.26.13, …). With best-match, every non-torch
#     package resolves to exactly the pure-PyPI version set (verified 2026-10-07
#     by diffing a PyPI-only compile), while torch itself can still only be
#     satisfied by the cu126 index because of its local label.
#   * diffusers AND transformers are installed from pinned git commits (per
#     PLAN M0.1 "exact git commits"): installing a "newer PyPI release
#     instead" would change the QwenImage21Pipeline interface that
#     docs/interfaces.md was surveyed against. NOTE: a requirements file
#     with VCS entries CANNOT be installed with `pip --require-hashes` —
#     pip cannot hash git repos. Install with `uv pip sync` only, which
#     builds the VCS wheels and enforces their recorded hashes.
#
# Regenerate requirements.lock exactly as recorded at the top of that file
# (uv pip compile, one run per supported interpreter; see docs/dependencies.md).

--extra-index-url https://download.pytorch.org/whl/cu126

torch==2.14.1+cu126
# Exact source commit per PLAN M0.1 (verified 2026-10-07: `git ls-remote
# …refs/tags/v5.17.0^{}` dereferences v5.17.0 — an annotated tag object
# 595ff117… that must NOT be pinned — to this commit; its __init__ reports
# __version__ = "5.17.0").
transformers @ git+https://github.com/huggingface/transformers.git@856157a2f3e9594954310df18fdccc31ffddebe9
# Pinned main commit (verified 2026-10-07; tree d77a3e3882af758d606ca22b53f63be8764e643a).
diffusers @ git+https://github.com/huggingface/diffusers.git@c6df88a511a98740646ee55577b590c9852650ce
# diffusers hard deps (would be pulled transitively; explicit for auditability):
safetensors
Pillow
# diffusers' torch/GGUF extras deps (device_map/offload plumbing; GGUF loader):
accelerate
gguf>=0.10.0
# Transitive of diffusers and transformers, pinned for interpreter uniformity:
# numpy 2.5.x requires Python >= 3.12, so an unpinned resolve picks 2.4.6 on
# 3.11 but 2.5.2 on 3.13. 2.4.6 is the newest numpy supporting both supported
# interpreters (requires-python >= 3.11), keeping one identical lock for both.
numpy==2.4.6
# Same uniformity reason (verified from PyPI metadata): networkx 3.7 is
# requires-python >=3.12, so an unpinned resolve picks 3.6.1 on 3.11 but 3.7
# on 3.13. 3.6.1 (>=3.11) is the newest version supporting both.
networkx==3.6.1
